#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541114 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69712d4c-92b7-5f9d-abcd-ca7ad46c6567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-s^2+10s+4}{s(s+1)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69712d4c-92b7-5f9d-abcd-ca7ad46c6567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-s^2+10s+4}{s(s+1)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540707} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8de0228-5ef5-53a6-b77b-949275d4025a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ca91093-1f1e-55da-a457-e3e1666bf899" :question/math-academy-id "q-333069" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{2}(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s+1}{s(s+2)}$ ." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{2}(t)+1\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-3 & =-2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+2){X}_{2}(s) & =3+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s+1}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s+1}{s(s+2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =4{X}_{2}(s)-1 \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =4(\\frac{3s+1}{s(s+2)})-1 \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4(3s+1)-s(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{12s+4-({s}^{2}+2s)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+10s+4}{s(s+2)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+10s+4}{s(s+2)(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+10s+4}{s(s+1)(s+2)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s+1}{s(s+2)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4b480b-46bc-5ad0-b2dc-179d612978aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2s^2-2s-6}{s(s-1)(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4b480b-46bc-5ad0-b2dc-179d612978aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2s^2-2s-6}{s(s-1)(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540741} :answer-field/id #uuid "1abf10fb-79e5-50b9-8eca-b49f881c098e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24075bbd-fad1-5e70-847c-3b96960e39c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333072" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3}{s(s+1)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{2}(t)+3\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0=-{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & =-{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2 & ={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =-2-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =-2-2(\\frac{3}{s(s+1)}) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2s(s+1)-6}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2({s}^{2}+s)-6}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-2s-6}{s(s+1)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-2s-6}{s(s+1)(s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-2s-6}{s(s-1)(s+1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3}{s(s+1)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "847ba49d-4395-5042-91bf-3d6b21b87fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "847ba49d-4395-5042-91bf-3d6b21b87fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306412} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5eac305-981a-52bc-8d2d-b02f36abb75f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "771c46b3-1f61-5283-9850-fe39ec331e05" :question/math-academy-id "q-333073" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{2}(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)} &=L{4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)} &=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+1}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0) &=4L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0) &=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+L{1}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 &=4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2 &=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+(\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-3)+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-3s+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff5d65f0-c6de-5048-a2be-21f61c684329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff5d65f0-c6de-5048-a2be-21f61c684329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540941} :answer-field/id #uuid "428707b6-8d94-52b6-9362-47c3559ec433" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e2e4b8f-9b19-50ef-87e0-50189c923190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{4t}+2e^{2t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e2e4b8f-9b19-50ef-87e0-50189c923190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{4t}+2e^{2t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540765} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbe9fab9-0798-54e1-b0d4-366304913f18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0823a96b-ef1d-57d5-85ea-8ef149bb4b9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-333132" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{2}(t)-4,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t}-{e}^{4\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =-{e}^{4t}+2{e}^{2t}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & ={e}^{4t}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{4t}+2{e}^{2t}+1 \\\\ {e}^{4t}+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7263ad0-8627-541d-bfc6-c16e5e4d797e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7263ad0-8627-541d-bfc6-c16e5e4d797e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307142} :answer-field/id #uuid "0499154a-ea02-54de-b962-e24efe7a857a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d49cc6-ba6d-59f6-b87f-809604383c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04d49cc6-ba6d-59f6-b87f-809604383c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305195} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff72e389-a584-56fe-9eb4-8d8f9751a7b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69893fe7-9a8d-5f16-833d-a445576651e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-333134" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}-2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
